# Cretli — design system UI/UX

One design system based on **Lit** and shared **tokens**. This rule applies when
creating or changing UI in `app_front/` and `public/`.

## 1. Tokens (`app_front/css/tokens.scss`)

Single source of truth: VS Code Dark+ palette, radius, spacing, typography,
motion as `--cr-*` on `:root` plus `body.theme-light` overrides.

- Dark palette: `--cr-bg #1e1e1e`, `--cr-surface #252526`, `--cr-border-strong
  #444`, `--cr-text #d4d4d4`, `--cr-text-muted #858585`, `--cr-accent #007acc`,
  `--cr-primary #094771` / `--cr-primary-hover #0d5a8f`, `--cr-error #f48771`,
  `--cr-success #4ec9b0`.
- Light (`body.theme-light`): `--cr-bg #f3f3f3`, `--cr-surface #e8e8e8`,
  `--cr-accent #006ab1`, `--cr-primary #006ab1`.
- Radius: `--cr-radius-sm 4px` (controls), `--cr-radius-md 6px` (dropdowns),
  `--cr-radius-lg 8px` (modals/cards).
- Spacing: `--cr-space-1…6` (0.25/0.5/0.75/1/1.5/2rem).
- Typography: `--cr-font-ui`, `--cr-font-mono`.
- Motion: `--cr-transition 120ms ease`.

**Rule:** Lit components use `var(--cr-*)` in `static styles`, not hardcoded
hex. Light theme via `:host-context(body.theme-light)`. Tokens are imported in
`app.scss` (`@use './tokens'`); pre-auth pages (login) import them from a
dedicated SCSS entry (e.g. `app_front/login/login.scss`).

## 2. Lit components (`app_front/components/ui/`)

`cr-*` registry of self-registering web components.

Conventions:
- Each file: `import { LitElement, css, html } from 'lit'`, class `CrXxx`, then
  `if (!customElements.get('cr-xxx')) customElements.define('cr-xxx', CrXxx)` +
  `export { CrXxx }`.
- **Shadow DOM** by default; styles in `static styles` with `var(--cr-*)` and
  `:host-context(body.theme-light)`.
- Reflect props when the attribute matters for CSS (`variant`, `disabled`,
  `open`).
- Inner controls expose `part="control"` (`cr-bar-button`, `cr-bar-input`) so
  padding/font can be styled from outside via `::part(control)` without breaking
  encapsulation.
- Custom events: `cr-<what>-change` / `cr-dialog-close`, with `bubbles: true,
  composed: true`.
- **Primitives with no app-level deps** (api, chat, logger) — reusable
  pre-auth.
- Barrel: `app_front/components/ui/index.js` (side-effect import of all
  `cr-*`). New screens import the barrel.
- MDI icons: `<span class="mdi mdi-<name>">` — **light DOM** (global `.mdi`
  from `@mdi/font` does not pierce Shadow DOM). Components take the icon via
  `<slot>` and style `::slotted(.mdi)`.

Available primitives: `cr-bar-button`, `cr-bar-input`, `cr-bar-textarea`,
`cr-bar-select`, `cr-dialog` (modal). `cr-todo-card`, `cr-sdk-block`,
`cr-sdk-mode-bar` — chat/TODO domain (state-dependent).

## 3. Modal — `<cr-dialog>`

Standard for new UI modals/dialogs. Shadow DOM, tokens, close via backdrop +
Escape, `cr-dialog-close` event.

API: props `open` (reflected), `heading`, `variant`, `persistent` (reflected —
blocks backdrop and Escape; use when the modal is the whole screen, e.g.
login); slots `icon`, `subheading`, default (body), `actions`; methods
`show()` / `hide()`.

The old utility `app_front/lib/modal.js` plus `.chat-settings-*` classes stay
for existing modals (`chat.js`, `App.js`, `filesPanel.js`, …). **New modals =
`cr-dialog`.** Incremental migration, not a big bang.

## 4. Forms

- Fields: `<cr-bar-input type="password|text" .value=? @input=>` (read
  `e.target.value` / `el.value`; native `input` is composed — it crosses
  shadow).
- Submit: `<cr-bar-button variant="primary" @click=>` + `fetch` (the button is
  `type="button"`; do not use native form submit).
- Validation: guard clauses; state on the component property (Lit reactive);
  error message in `.message[data-tone="error"]`.
- Messages: `data-tone="error" | "success"`.

## 5. Theme

- `app_front/theme.js`: `localStorage('cretli-theme')` =
  `dark|light|system`; `theme-light` class on `<body>`. Legacy key
  `cursor-remote-theme` is still read via `storageKeyAlias.js`.
- Standalone pages (pre-auth, no SPA): inline **anti-FOUC** script that reads
  `localStorage` and sets `body.theme-light` before render.
- `<meta name="theme-color">`: `#1e1e1e` (dark) / `#f3f3f3` (light) — match
  `--cr-bg`, not GitHub `#0d1117`.

## 6. Pre-auth entry pattern (e.g. login)

Pages required before auth do **not** load the full SPA (`App.js`, xterm,
chat). Pattern:

- Separate **webpack entry** (e.g. `login: './login/LoginApp.js'`) in
 `webpack.dev.js` + `webpack.prod.js`. `splitChunks` gives it its **own**
 `vendor-login.bundle.js` (Lit + UI primitives only) — it must not share
 `vendor.bundle.js` with the SPA, which carries xterm, markdown-it and the
 icon font. Pre-auth pages also skip `vendor.css`; inline an SVG instead of
 pulling in `@mdi/font` for a couple of icons.
- Entry imports: `components/ui/index.js` (barrel), `theme.js`, its own SCSS
  with `@use '../css/tokens'` (tokens on the page).
- The page component uses **light DOM** (`createRenderRoot() { return this }`)
  so global `.mdi` and tokens from the entry CSS work.
- Server: `/login` and `/dist/app/*` assets are public pre-auth (`lib/auth.js`
  `requireAuth`); login API is on the whitelist (`/api/auth-status`,
  `/api/setup`, `/api/login`).
- `public/sw.js`: add the page bundle and CSS to `SHELL_ASSETS` (offline PWA).

## 7. Migration rule

- **New UI = Lit + tokens.** Do not invent new standalone designs (like the old
  `login.html` with a GitHub palette).
- Existing plain HTML + global SCSS (`header`, `tabs`, panels,
  `.chat-settings-*`) stays; migrate incrementally, file by file, as separate
  tasks — not a big bang.
- Do not duplicate tokens as hardcoded hex in new components — use
  `var(--cr-*)`.
